    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "psbt: analyzepsbt reports an error when outputs exceed inputs",
    "user": {
      "login": "Ravan002",
      "id": 95362051,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBa8cAw",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95362051?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Ravan002",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Ravan002/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`AnalyzePSBT` computes `fee = in_amt - out_amt` once every input amount is known and returns it as is. A PSBT whose outputs are worth more than its inputs therefore gets a negative `fee` and a `next` role of updater, even though no wallet can ever sign it into a valid transaction. The function already returns `PSBT is not valid. ...` for bad input values, unspendable outputs and an out-of-range output total.\n\nAn output total above the input total is reported the same way:\n\n```\nbefore: {\"fee\": -1.00000000, \"next\": \"updater\", ...}\nafter:  {\"next\": \"creator\", \"error\": \"PSBT is not valid. Output amount larger than input amount\"}\n```\n\nThe functional test builds a PSBT that spends a 1 BTC output into a 2 BTC output and checks the error and the `creator` role. Without the change the assertion on `next` fails. `rpc_psbt.py`, `wallet_send.py`, `wallet_multisig_descriptor_psbt.py`, `rpc_openrpc.py` and the psbt unit tests pass.\n\n",
